From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:17:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: Sable dark palette, focus outline and type scale for
 Contacts

The Sable People design (sable-contacts-people-titan2) is dark only.
Contacts now uses one dark palette whatever the system light/dark
setting, instead of light themes that the platform force-darkens:

* sable_colors.xml carries the Sable dark tokens (the same values as
  Phone). The accent is not hard-coded: primary_color, the accent of
  both themes, is system_accent1_200 from the system palette, which
  the Sable accent seeds.
* PeopleTheme, PeopleThemeAppCompat, the launch, dialog and helper
  themes inherit the dark Material/AppCompat themes, never
  force-darken, and every colour resource with a light value points
  at a token: near-black list and detail background, raised panels for
  cards, popups, dialogs, the search box and the selection bar, light
  text, outline-tone dividers, dark status and navigation bars. The
  -night colours and launch screen are removed, as they would now
  repeat the defaults.
* The toolbar is a flat bar on the page background (sable_toolbar_color,
  elevation already 0) with the title in the design's ScreenTitle size
  (22sp medium). PeopleActivity and MaterialColorMapUtils paint the bar
  with sable_toolbar_color instead of primary_color, which is now the
  accent (two lines; group colours are resources).
* Focus: the list selector and the theme's selectableItemBackground are
  the Sable row background, a ripple on touch and a 2dp accent outline
  around a dark accent fill while the row or action has keyboard or
  trackpad focus. This covers the People list, search results, Quick
  Contact entries and the editor rows.
* Section letters (22sp light from the earlier patch) are drawn in the
  accent; directory headers are the Sable section label (12sp, caps,
  accent). The empty-state "Add contact" button is an outlined pill.

Focus order, touch targets, the A-Z rail and keys, the route subtitle,
the Hub chip and every upstream function are unchanged.
